# Elmo for Umbrel - provider configuration.
#
# Copy this file to config.env in the same directory, then restart the app
# from Umbrel (or `sudo ~/umbrel/scripts/app restart ausilio-elmo`):
#
#   cp ~/umbrel/app-data/ausilio-elmo/config.env.example \
#      ~/umbrel/app-data/ausilio-elmo/config.env
#
# config.env is not part of the app package, so it survives updates. The file
# is sourced as shell, and either the upstream names shown below or an APP_ELMO_
# prefix works (e.g. APP_ELMO_OPENROUTER_API_KEY).
#
# Minimum setup: one direct LLM key. It runs brand onboarding and the
# Opportunities report, and an OpenRouter key also calls Jev to judge mentions.
# Elmo's dashboard shows a "missing environment configuration" page until its
# required configuration (a provider key plus SCRAPE_TARGETS) is available.
#
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
#
# That one key tracks Claude through OpenRouter, judges answers through Jev,
# and covers onboarding. For a wider picture add a scraper key (which tracks
# the live ChatGPT / Google AI Mode / Perplexity / Copilot surfaces) and/or
# more direct model keys.
#
# SCRAPE_TARGETS is derived from the first configured provider in this order:
#   BrightData, Cloro, SearchApi, Olostep, Oxylabs, DataForSEO,
#   OpenRouter, Anthropic, OpenAI, Mistral
# Set SCRAPE_TARGETS explicitly to track a different set of models.

# --- Direct LLM APIs (at least one) ---
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# --- Jev mention judge (https://console.typesafe.ai) ---
# The worker will not start without TYPESAFE_API_KEY or OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
# When both are set, TypeSafe is used directly.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# --- Scrapers (optional, one or more) ---
# BRIGHTDATA_API_TOKEN=
# CLORO_API_KEY=
# SEARCHAPI_API_KEY=
# OLOSTEP_API_KEY=
# OXYLABS_USERNAME=
# OXYLABS_PASSWORD=
# DATAFORSEO_LOGIN=
# DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD=

# --- Optional tuning ---
# SCRAPE_TARGETS=chatgpt:brightdata:online,google-ai-mode:brightdata:online
# ONBOARDING_LLM_TARGET=claude:anthropic-api
# REPROCESS_DAYS=90
# RUNS_PER_PROMPT=5
# DEFAULT_DELAY_HOURS=24
# JINA_API_KEY=
# After restoring a database from another device, put that device's
# ELMO_ENCRYPTION_KEY (from its exports.env) here so stored credentials stay
# readable; new credentials use this device's derived key.
# ELMO_ENCRYPTION_KEY_OLD=

# Telemetry is disabled by default (exports.sh sets DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1 and
# DO_NOT_TRACK=1).
# DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1

# Public URL. Leave unset to keep http://localhost:8096, which is what Elmo
# needs internally for MCP and still allows LAN access. Set it to your HTTPS
# origin only when serving Elmo through a reverse proxy / HTTPS domain; MCP
# then advertises that URL and sign-in is restricted to it.
# APP_URL=https://elmo.example.com
